From: SenkOS
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: put the display engine behind
 the IOMMU

The display engine is the IOMMU's master 0, as on the H6, whose mixer0
has had "iommus = <&iommu 0>" for years. Without it the mixers can only
scan out physically contiguous buffers: a GPU (panfrost) buffer is
scattered pages, so the display driver can't import it ("gbm bo get
handle failed" in Weston) and the compositor copies every client frame
on the GPU instead of putting it on a plane. With the GPU busy that copy
misses vblanks (Super Mario 64 at 40 fps). sun8i_mixer makes mixer0 the
DMA device for the whole pipeline, so mixer0 is the one that needs it.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@
 					 <&display_clocks CLK_MIXER0>;
 				clock-names = "bus", "mod";
 				resets = <&display_clocks RST_MIXER0>;
+				iommus = <&iommu 0>;
 				allwinner,planes = <&planes>;
 
 				ports {
